1. Abstract
Customer churn refers to customers discontinuing a service. In subscription-based telecommunications, understanding churn patterns can help organizations monitor customer segments and design data-informed retention activities. This project uses the IBM Telco Customer Churn sample dataset to perform data cleaning, exploratory data analysis, visualization and supervised machine learning.
2. Problem Statement
The objective is to analyze customer characteristics associated with observed churn and demonstrate a machine-learning workflow that predicts the churn class from available customer attributes.
3. Objectives
    • Understand the structure and quality of the customer dataset.
    • Clean and preprocess numerical and categorical variables.
    • Explore churn patterns using descriptive statistics and visualizations.
    • Compare observed churn rates across contract, service, payment and tenure segments.
    • Build Logistic Regression and Decision Tree classification models.
    • Evaluate models using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score and ROC-AUC.
    • Translate analytical outputs into clear business-oriented observations.
4. Dataset Description
The project uses the public IBM Telco Customer Churn sample dataset. It contains 7,043 customer records and 21 columns. The target variable is Churn, which indicates whether a customer left the service. The dataset contains demographic, service, account, contract, payment and billing attributes.
Category	Examples	Purpose
Customer profile	gender, SeniorCitizen, Partner, Dependents	Customer characteristics
Services	InternetService, TechSupport, StreamingTV	Service usage
Account	tenure, Contract, PaymentMethod	Account relationship
Billing	MonthlyCharges, TotalCharges	Financial attributes
Target	Churn	Classification outcome
